# RED-ON-RUST — REPOSITORY BOOTSTRAP PACK
 
## Status
 `Architecture:       FROZEN Specification:      FROZEN Verification:       FROZEN Repository Design:  BOOTSTRAP BASELINE Implementation:     READY ` 
This document defines the initial Rust workspace, crate boundaries, dependency direction, visibility rules, module layout, testing topology, and implementation sequence.
 
It does **not** introduce new language semantics.
  
# 1. Repository Objective
 
The repository must make the following architectural property difficult to violate accidentally:
 
[ \boxed{ Untrusted\ Input \not\Rightarrow Authority \not\Rightarrow External\ Effect } ]
 
and:
 
[ \boxed{ Production\ Semantics \neq Reference\ Implementation } ]
 
The workspace therefore separates:
 `untrusted language data         ↓ compiler         ↓ trusted executable representation         ↓ machine         ↓ authority / resources         ↓ durable effects         ↓ host ` 
while independently maintaining:
 `production implementation         ↕ normalized observations         ↕ independent reference model `  
