# 36. First Security Gate
 
Before implementing external effects, demonstrate:
 
[ \boxed{ Block \not\Rightarrow ExecutablePlan } ]
 
and:
 
[ \boxed{ CapRef \not\Rightarrow AuthorityInspection } ]
 
and:
 
[ \boxed{ Value::Capability \not\Rightarrow OrdinaryMessageTransfer } ]
 
and:
 
[ \boxed{ HostInvocation \Rightarrow DurableIssued } ]
 
These are repository-level architectural properties, not merely test cases.
  
# 37. First Differential Gate
 
Before actors or effects exist, require:
 `Production CEK        ↓ Normalized Observation        ↑ Reference CEK ` 
to agree for:
 `Value Var Let Seq If Lambda Call ` 
including faults.
 
The differential harness should be operational before the production CEK becomes large.
  
# 38. Repository-Level Definition of Done
 
A component is complete only when:
 `implementation + unit tests + reference semantics + differential tests + obligation mapping + mutation coverage + documentation ` 
are present where applicable.
 
"Code compiles" is not completion.
 
"Unit tests pass" is not completion.
 
"Coverage is high" is not completion.
 
The final standard is independent semantic agreement plus verification evidence.
  
# 39. Final Repository Invariant
 
The repository should make this architecture visible:
 `             UNTRUSTED                 │         ┌───────▼────────┐         │ Block / LLM    │         └───────┬────────┘                 │           compiler only                 │         ┌───────▼────────┐         │ ExecutablePlan │         └───────┬────────┘                 │         ┌───────▼────────┐         │ CEK Runtime    │         └───┬────────┬───┘             │        │             ▼        ▼        Capability   Budget           Kernel     System             │        │             └────┬───┘                  ▼           Effect Issuance                  │           durable boundary                  │                  ▼               Host ` 
and independently:
